From 88a240d86d3d64521f9194abe185ac71cc74d0bd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: wcn36xx: fix heap overflow from oversized firmware HAL response

The firmware response dispatcher copies all synchronous HAL responses
into the 4096-byte hal_buf without validating the response length. A
response exceeding WCN36XX_HAL_BUF_SIZE causes a heap buffer overflow
with firmware-controlled content.

Backport of mainline 88a240d86d, context adjusted for SET_THERMAL_MITIGATION_RSP
(patch 453).
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/wcn36xx/smd.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/wcn36xx/smd.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/wcn36xx/smd.c
@@ -3391,6 +3391,10 @@
 	case WCN36XX_HAL_UPDATE_CHANNEL_LIST_RSP:
 	case WCN36XX_HAL_ADD_BCN_FILTER_RSP:
 	case WCN36XX_HAL_SET_THERMAL_MITIGATION_RSP:
+		if (len > WCN36XX_HAL_BUF_SIZE) {
+			wcn36xx_warn("HAL response too large: %d\n", len);
+			break;
+		}
 		memcpy(wcn->hal_buf, buf, len);
 		wcn->hal_rsp_len = len;
 		complete(&wcn->hal_rsp_compl);
